# Silverquill, the Disputant ("Each instant and sorcery spell you cast has casualty 1") on turn 1 and Raiding Schemes ("Each
# noncreature spell you cast has conspire") on turn 3 give Lightning Bolt casualty and then conspire, in the order of their
# timestamps (CR 613.7). Bot1 pays casualty by sacrificing Silverquill itself and declines conspire (CR 601.2b). The Bolt
# loses casualty as Silverquill leaves (CR 611.3a), so when it becomes cast it has no casualty to trigger (CR 601.2i, 702.153b),
# and the conspire it still has was not paid (CR 702.78b): nothing copies it. The Bolt alone hits Bot2: 20-3 = 17.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Ruby
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Silverquill, the Disputant
Raiding Schemes
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x30

